# No agent credit

Commits, pull requests, patches and files in this repository must not credit an AI agent.

- No `Co-Authored-By`, `Generated-by`, session-link or similar trailers naming an agent or a tool.
- No "Generated with ..." lines in PR descriptions.
- The commit author is the human owner of the repository. Do not set an agent as author or committer.
- Before applying a patch from outside (`git am`), read its headers. If they credit an agent, do not apply it as-is: copy the content you want and commit it under the owner's name.
